url: "https://github.com/yyyyyyzt/HARK-Human-Gated-Authority-Typed-Review-Knowledge"
title: "HARK: Authority-Typed Review Knowledge for Evidence-Bearing Document Review"
abstract: >-
  Paper and artifact for HARK, a review system for evidence-bearing document review. Review rules
  carry an operational authority: hard rules are decided by deterministic verifiers that also produce
  located absence records (a model may never assert absence); hybrid rules let verifiers locate a
  span while the model judges only inside it; soft rules only raise pending items. A located-quote
  gate qualifies submitted evidence, a deterministic policy derives the suggested verdict, and expert
  dispositions are stored as decision records. The artifact contains the manuscript and submission
  materials, the extension-package source, the 28-rule package, the 100-proposal synthetic corpus
  with 253 planted defects, the ablation runner, and the nine published evaluation runs. Certified
  human approval, an effective authority cap across all write paths, and content-addressed
  configuration restore are target contracts, not implemented guarantees.
